      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ZBYS",
      "code_hash": "0ba1b54611464f266ec99242d47741a6",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "aLJB",
      "code_hash": "6ba210297394d45088f4b30d1664c5ec",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nHfw",
      "code_hash": "42f1c10685056d775a1e91f48cff7d32",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "xXTn",
      "code_hash": "c7ba51c0930fbfc50a019a7d72e3a3d4",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "AjVT",
      "code_hash": "f478b86c39554b201107848161a8ca97",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"project-and-contract-color\">Project and contract color</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Write the color-averaged numerator as <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(C_{\\rm color}\\,\\widehat N||)</marimo-tex>.\nAll subsequent numerator and UV expressions show <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\widehat N||)</marimo-tex> with\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(C_{\\rm color}||)</marimo-tex> kept outside. If a vertex has several color structures,\ntheir relative coefficients remain in <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\widehat N||)</marimo-tex>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "pHFh",
      "code_hash": "8cf2ad20e2bd052c8de676e7c223e91a",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "NCOB",
      "code_hash": "767ca4addec5ecaf14e7b5e4824a0ea0",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "aqbW",
      "code_hash": "6cfd8467336c623e5ceb8b0efa5e86e2",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"collect-bispinor-chains\">Collect bispinor chains</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Choose a diagram containing a bottom-quark line in <strong>Particles in the loop</strong>\nto see slash notation: <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\not{q}=\\gamma^\\mu q_\\mu||)</marimo-tex>.\nThis view collects the bispinor factors into ordered chains and traces,\nleaving the Dirac traces unevaluated.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "TRpd",
      "code_hash": "2db60377396d79b8bf53e6f45c7866b2",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "TXez",
      "code_hash": "835b4d71efa3d50609ae5be5d5cfe539",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "dNNg",
      "code_hash": null,
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "yCnT",
      "code_hash": "baefc2c44117f9664a726ac987b4ed4e",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"project-the-external-lorentz-indices\">Project the external Lorentz indices</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Color has already been averaged. For off-shell <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p^2\\ne0||)</marimo-tex>, use\n$<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\mathcal P_{\\mu\\nu}=\n\\frac{1}{D-1}\n\\left(g_{\\mu\\nu}-\\frac{p_\\mu p_\\nu}{p^2}\\right).||)</marimo-tex>$\nIt extracts <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p^2\\Pi_T||)</marimo-tex> from\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||((p^2g^{\\mu\\nu}-p^\\mu p^\\nu)\\Pi_T||)</marimo-tex>.\nThis replaces the default external polarization vectors; it is not an\nadditional polarization sum. The helper reads the actual external slots.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "wlCL",
      "code_hash": "8600c50b67055151a18830cd10f7f471",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "kqZH",
      "code_hash": "9e274aa0ef07e6ec8b03f4f8f84ea4a8",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "wAgl",
      "code_hash": "e4cfb54468201ea98c4d11f57e2913e9",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "rEll",
      "code_hash": "dc3f8efd40b8c614e3f3f277bd193f35",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "dGlV",
      "code_hash": "fcd6e556fcb4ac6e00134a9a91eeede4",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The last expression includes the symmetry factor and closed-loop signs,\nwith the model couplings expressed through <code>UFO::G</code>. The global\n<code>color_factor</code> remains separate from this expression and the UV steps.\nThe native graph factor already includes the Grassmann minus for each\nclosed ghost loop; <code>diagram_weight</code> evaluates it without an extra sign.\nAll algebra functions are defined in the notebook cells above.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The cells below expand an expression copy, apply FeynKit's tensor reduction,\nand compute the integrated UV counterterm.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "SdmI",
      "code_hash": "8200009cc623c80f939a9da28246c2f6",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"build-the-energy-denominators\">Build the energy denominators</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>build_cff()</code> constructs the Cross-Free Family representation of this\ndiagram. Its output is a normal Symbolica expression. This step constructs\nthe denominators; it does not evaluate the loop integral.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "lgWD",
      "code_hash": "e1b63e28fa349555343b2567736a4ac8",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "yOPj",
      "code_hash": "468f3bc5bd80d5fe5a7016d5d086f593",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"uv-expansion-on-a-copy-of-the-expression\">UV expansion on a copy of the expression</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Read each internal edge's mass from the model and use\nthe graph's momentum routing. Here <code>prop(q, M2)</code> denotes <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(1/(q^2-M^2)||)</marimo-tex>.\nCopy the projected integrand with <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(C_{\\rm color}||)</marimo-tex> kept outside and scale\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(k\\to k/t||)</marimo-tex> in numerator and propagators together.\nAfter extracting <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(t^2||)</marimo-tex> from each propagator, apply\n$<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\operatorname{prop}(k+tp,t^2m^2)\\longrightarrow\n\\operatorname{prop}(k+tp,t^2m^2+(1-t^2)m_{\\rm UV}^2).||)</marimo-tex>$\nAt <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(t=1||)</marimo-tex> this recovers the physical integrand; at <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(t=0||)</marimo-tex> the denominator is\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(k^2-m_{\\rm UV}^2||)</marimo-tex>. Include the loop-measure factor <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(t^{-4L}||)</marimo-tex> for\nfour-dimensional power counting and expand through <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(t^0||)</marimo-tex>. For these\nquadratically divergent bubbles, the series starts at <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(t^{-2}||)</marimo-tex>.\nRemove the measure factor before tensor reduction to recover the\ncounterterm integrand. This bookkeeping does not change the symbolic\ndimension <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D||)</marimo-tex> used in the contractions.\nAll momentum squares remain dot products, including <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p\\cdot p||)</marimo-tex>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "fwwy",
      "code_hash": "7022a3ca5c457acde770584dffa6ae17",
      "outputs": [],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "LJZf",
      "code_hash": "c38c8b778b462e552842671264a3a14a",
